this is an orchestra rehearsal  and these young conductors can't  actually hear the music  for kids with hearing impairments  entering the world of classical music  can be a daunting experience  but this berlin-based orchestra is  breaking that barrier  they have been introducing classical  music to kids who are deaf or hard of  hearing  for the past eight years i'm christian  harvest and i play the violin in the  mala chamber orchestra  field music is a project we have with  hearing impaired children  we have been in hong kong we were in  rome we were  in london through classes and workshops  kids learn music on their own terms  using sensors other than  sound like touching the instruments as  they vibrate  and feeling the rhythm of the percussion  through the floor  or even by simply watching the musicians  play  some of them tell us why you make weird  faces when you play the violin  you enter the music so it can be painful  it can be really  really joyful it's very intensive  and the kids of course react much more  on that because that's their language  others totally moved and tell me that  it's the most beautiful thing they've  done  [Music]  [Applause]  at the end of the program the kids are  put in charge as the conductors for a  day  kids like mara who can only hear with  the assistance of a hearing aid  my name is  i feel very moved actually i start  crying  oh am really happy to see how  how moved these kids are by simple  things  with the music  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

